    "WattNode Revenue Modbus"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
  "applies_to": "WattNode Modbus WNC and revenue RWNC models, firmware 18-24, per manual WNC-MB-1.18c (2015-11-03).",
  "summary": "The WattNode Modbus is a compact three-phase energy meter with external CTs and an RS-485 Modbus RTU port. Most values come both as 32-bit floats and as scaled integers; 32-bit values are sent low word first. This map covers energy (net, positive, negative, reactive, apparent), power, voltage, current, PF, frequency, demand, CT and demand configuration, communication overrides and diagnostics.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The manual documents registers one-based and says they are sent zero-based: EnergySum is documented at 1001 and appears on the bus as 1000 (0x03E8). Wire address = documented number - 1."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": "18-24",
  "source": {
    "title": "WattNode Modbus Installation and Operation Manual",
    "doc_number": "WNC-MB-1.18c",
    "revision_date": "2015-11-03",
    "url": "https://ctlsys.com/m/WNC-MB-Ref-Manual.pdf",
    "pages": "Addressing and 32-bit order pp. 32-33; register lists pp. 34-39; baud DIP p. 20; model codes p. 52"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Word order: the manual says the first (lower) register of a float or 32-bit integer holds the least significant 16 bits (little-endian, 'byte order 1032' on Tridium), so 32-bit values are CDAB.",
    "Holding and input registers are interchangeable (functions 03 and 04 return the same data).",
    "Left out: ConfigPasscode (1601-1602, signedness not stated); integer power, current and demand registers (1209-1212, 1343-1360), which use the configurable PowerIntScale/CurrentIntScale factors; integer per-phase energies; gain/phase adjustment, creep and I/O mode settings; option information and custom register map registers.",
    "Read both halves of a 32-bit value in one request; the meter only guarantees a consistent pair within a single read.",
    "The Model register lists codes only for WNC models; revenue RWNC codes are not given.",
    "SerialNumber, UptimeSecs and TotalSecs are described as 32-bit long integers, which the manual defines as signed, so they are INT32."
  ],
